\begin{align*}
  \sum \binom{a_i}{2} & \geq n \binom{\frac{\sum a_i}{n}}{2} 
  & \geq n\binom{\frac {kr}n}{2} 
\end{align*}
Now, AFTSOC each intersection between 2 subsets has less that  $r - \frac{nk}{4(k - 1)}.$  Thus, we have that the total number of common elements is also   $$ < \binom k2 \left(r - \frac{nk}{4(k - 1)}\right) $$  Thus, 
